**"Evaluation Period"** means the period beginning when the Licensee first compiles, executes, or otherwise runs the Software for a particular Evaluation and ending sixty (60) calendar days thereafter, unless the Licensor agrees in writing to a longer period.

Merely obtaining, downloading, cloning, viewing, or inspecting the source code without compiling, executing, or otherwise running the Software does not begin the Evaluation Period.

A new download, copy, installation, version, release, environment, employee, contractor, or substantially similar assessment does not restart or extend an Evaluation Period for the same contemplated use.

**"Evaluation"** means temporary, non-operational use of the Software during the applicable Evaluation Period solely and directly to assess its functionality, suitability, compatibility, performance, security, reliability, or fitness for a contemplated use, including to decide whether to obtain a separate license.

Evaluation may include compiling, executing, testing, benchmarking, auditing, inspecting, or integrating the Software in a test or proof-of-concept environment only to the extent reasonably necessary to conduct that assessment.

Evaluation does not include:

(a) use of the Software to perform an actual production, business, organizational, administrative, infrastructure, service-delivery, customer-facing, or other operational function;

(b) use of the Software as a substitute, whether temporary or permanent, for software or services that would otherwise perform such a function;

(c) use of the Software to process or support a live or ongoing workload, except to the minimum extent reasonably necessary to reproduce or simulate that workload solely for Evaluation;

(d) use of the Software to provide any product, service, result, output, or other benefit to a third party as part of an actual service or operational activity;

(e) recurring or ongoing use after the assessment for which the Software was being evaluated has reasonably concluded; or

(f) compiling, executing, or otherwise running the Software after expiration of the applicable Evaluation Period, unless permitted by a separate written agreement with the Licensor or by mandatory applicable law.

**"Commercial Use"** means use of the Software in connection with a trade, business, profession, paid engagement, revenue-generating activity, commercial product or service, or internal business process. Evaluation permitted by Section 3 is not Commercial Use.

**"Production Use"** means use of the Software in a live or deployed environment where the Software, or results produced by it, are relied upon to provide functionality, processing, infrastructure, or services to actual users, customers, employees, systems, devices, or operational processes. Evaluation is not Production Use.

**"Operational Use"** means recurring, ongoing, or otherwise non-evaluative use of the Software as part of the actual activities, administration, infrastructure, workflows, service delivery, or other operations of any person or organization, whether commercial or non-commercial.

Use does not cease to be Evaluation merely because it is performed by or on infrastructure belonging to a business, university, research institution, nonprofit organization, public authority, or other organization, provided that the use otherwise satisfies the definition of Evaluation.

Automated build, continuous-integration, or similar automated execution of the Software is permitted only where reasonably necessary for an activity permitted by Section 3 and is not itself part of a production, deployment, service-delivery, or operational workflow.

